- Added Omarchy as a recognized Linux platform. Omarchy 4 ("quattro") ships its own `/etc/os-release` with `ID=omarchy`, where earlier versions inherited `ID=arch` from Arch Linux, so Fleet stopped recognizing these hosts as Linux. Host vitals (private IP address, MAC address, disk space, uptime, fleetd version, users) and software inventory now populate, disk encryption and key escrow are available, policies and labels scoped to `linux` target these hosts, and **Run script** is available from the host actions dropdown. Omarchy hosts continue to roll up onto the "Arch Linux" / "rolling" row in the OS inventory.
